Subject: [PATCH] Connect native whole-file requests to NL read failure and shutdown
Upstream-base: 4a9ab8151d9a74e321e52b36c95d1e157d41af60

The native port provides nlLoadEntireFileAsync/nlCancelEntireFileLoad in
src/runtime/whole_file.cpp. Keep original console implementations unselected:
they truncate pointers into 32-bit handles and mix host delete with game-arena
records. Native opaque tokens preserve existing game handle fields; the adapter
uses host-owned records, explicit MEM1/MEM2 or borrowed output ownership, and
per-request cancellation callbacks.

Abort a failed whole-file request from the manager's shared Service method,
including synchronous reads that service it, without aborting other loads.
Close/drain owned files before releasing buffers, and release pending records
before destroying the raw manager or game arenas. Document the native API,
including cancellation joining busy workers and ownership at callback entry.

This adds no compression, bundle/cache, original INI parsing, or graphics stubs.
All source edits remain in generated copies. Console behavior is unchanged.

diff --git a/include/NL/nlFile.h b/include/NL/nlFile.h
index 57cc6ec..0be5afa 100644
--- a/include/NL/nlFile.h
+++ b/include/NL/nlFile.h
@@ -47,6 +47,17 @@ void nlRead(nlFile* file, void* buffer, unsigned int size, unsigned long bufferS
 void nlClose(nlFile* file);
 bool nlFileExists(const char* filename);
 void* nlLoadEntireFile(const char* filename, unsigned long* outSize, unsigned int alignment, eAllocType type, void* buffer, unsigned long bufferSize, MemoryAllocator* allocator);
+#ifdef MSCHARGED_NATIVE
+// Native whole-file handles are opaque, nonrecycled 32-bit tokens, not pointers.
+// Missing files return 0 without a callback; empty files call back inline with
+// null/0 and return 0. Other completions run on the NL servicing thread and pass
+// the logical length. Allocated output transfers to the callback; supplied output
+// is always borrowed. A zero supplied capacity means the caller guarantees the
+// logical file length. Read/submission failures throw without a success callback.
+// Cancellation joins native workers, even while busy. Its callback borrows the
+// data and receives the original completion callback; only owned data is freed.
+// Completed/cancelled/unknown tokens return false. Shutdown drains without callbacks.
+#endif
 unsigned int nlLoadEntireFileAsync(const char* filename, LoadAsyncCallback callback, void* userData, unsigned int alignment, eAllocType type, void* buffer, unsigned long bufferSize, MemoryAllocator* allocator);
 bool nlCancelEntireFileLoad(unsigned int handle, void (*callback)(void*, unsigned long, void*, LoadAsyncCallback));
 
